#~ msgid "English"
#~ msgstr "Saesneg"

#~ msgid "Welsh"
#~ msgstr "Cymraeg"

#~ msgid "show on map"
#~ msgstr "dangos ar y map"

#~ msgid ""
#~ "This 100-hole rock cannon tucked away in Parc Meurig is being reclaimed "
#~ "by nature, with its bored holes and carved-out interconnecting grooves "
#~ "almost all covered over by a layer of moss and grass."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "Mae'r canon carreg 100 twll hwn sydd wedi'i guddio ym Mharc Meurig yn "
#~ "cael ei adfer gan natur, gyda'i dyllau diflas a'i rigolau cydgysylltiedig "
#~ "wedi'u cerfio bron i gyd wedi'u gorchuddio gan haen o fwsogl a glaswellt."

#~ msgid "Rock Cannon, Mynydd Llandegai"
#~ msgstr "Carreg Cannon, Mynydd Llandegai"

#~ msgid "Rock cannon, looking east towards Penrhyn Quarry and the Carneddau."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "Cannon craig, yn edrych tua'r dwyrain tuag at Chwarel y Penrhyn a'r "
#~ "Carneddau."

#~ msgid "Rock Cannons of Gwynedd"
#~ msgstr "Creigiau Cannan Gwynedd"

#~ msgid ""
#~ "Discovering the unique tradition of celebration carved into the landscape "
#~ "of Gwynedd and Wales."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "Darganfod y traddodiad unigryw o ddathlu sydd wedi'i gerfio yn nhirwedd "
#~ "Gwynedd a Chymru."

#~ msgid "All about Rock Cannons"
#~ msgstr "Popeth am Greigiau Cannan"

#~ msgid ""
#~ "A rock cannon is a method of salutation and the celebration of important "
#~ "social, commercial and industrial events, whether they are of local or "
#~ "national interest, that dates back as far as the latter years of the 18th "
#~ "century. It was initially believed that this method of celebration was "
#~ "confined to the slate quarries and metal mines of Gwynedd, but research "
#~ "has now shown that sites exist in other parts of North Wales. As of 2001, "
#~ "235 sites have been found adding up to 6,157 holes."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "Mae canon craig yn ddull o gyfarch a dathlu digwyddiadau cymdeithasol, "
#~ "masnachol a diwydiannol pwysig, boed o ddiddordeb lleol neu genedlaethol, "
#~ "sy'n dyddio'n ôl cyn belled â blynyddoedd olaf y 18fed ganrif. Credwyd yn "
#~ "wreiddiol bod y dull hwn o ddathlu wedi'i gyfyngu i chwareli llechi a "
#~ "mwyngloddiau metel Gwynedd, ond mae ymchwil bellach wedi dangos bod "
#~ "safleoedd yn bodoli mewn rhannau eraill o Ogledd Cymru. Hyd at 2001, mae "
#~ "235 o safleoedd wedi'u canfod yn cyfateb i 6,157 o dyllau."

#~ msgid "Fun facts about Rock Cannons"
#~ msgstr "Ffeithiau hwyl am Ganonau Creigiau"

#~ msgid ""
#~ "The earliest record of cannon in Gwynedd is found in a contemporary "
#~ "newspaper report (1808), which gives lengthy details of the celebration "
#~ "in various areas of present Gwynedd of the 50th anniversary of George "
#~ "III's accession to the throne. It states, under the heading of JUBILEE "
#~ "that 'In no part of the British Empire has this event been celebrated "
#~ "with greater demonstrations of rejoicing, thankfulness, and all the more "
#~ "estimable virtues of charity and beneficence, than in this principality'. "
#~ "Rock cannons were used to celebrate the marriage of Albert Edward, Prince "
#~ "of Wales to Princess Alexandra of Denmark in 1863 as well as the Diamond "
#~ "Jubilee of Queen Victoria in 1897."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "Mae'r cofnod cynharaf o ganon yng Ngwynedd i'w gael mewn adroddiad papur "
#~ "newydd cyfoes (1808), sy'n rhoi manylion hir am y dathliad mewn gwahanol "
#~ "ardaloedd o Wynedd bresennol o 50fed pen-blwydd esgyniad Siôr III i'r "
#~ "orsedd. Mae'n nodi, o dan y pennawd JIWBILI 'Nid yw'r digwyddiad hwn "
#~ "wedi'i ddathlu mewn unrhyw ran o Ymerodraeth Prydain gyda mwy o "
#~ "arddangosiadau o lawenydd, diolchgarwch, a holl rinweddau mwy gwerthfawr "
#~ "elusen a charedigrwydd, nag yn y dywysogaeth hon'. Defnyddiwyd canonau "
#~ "craig i ddathlu priodas Albert Edward, Tywysog Cymru â'r Dywysoges "
#~ "Alexandra o Ddenmarc ym 1863 yn ogystal â Jiwbilî Diemwnt y Frenhines "
#~ "Victoria ym 1897."
